# generation: 1
# nodes.tsv - every machine this system will ever talk to, by address.
#
# There is no name column, on purpose. This machine sits OUTSIDE the PVE
# cluster, so it has neither the cluster's /etc/hosts nor its DNS, and an
# address that only works while a name server answers is an address that stops
# working during the exact incident this tool exists for. PVE node names are
# still needed to write a guest config - they are discovered from the cluster
# and cached in nodes.map, which nobody edits by hand.
#
# TAB separated; lines starting with # are ignored. role is one of:
#   storage   the node the engines run on, and where the images live
#   backup    holds the stopped DR copies and PBS. Everything leans on this one:
#             the config sync, the node-name discovery, and every question a
#             failback asks about a production CT
#   compute   mounts the images over NFS and runs the containers. No ssh from
#             here is expected or needed - they are asked through the cluster API
#
# ip	role
10.100.1.17	storage
10.100.1.9	backup
10.100.1.28	compute
10.100.1.32	compute
10.100.1.33	compute
